{%- comment -%}
  The circular colour chip beside a colour option's label.

  A flat colour only -- never the variant's photograph. Shopify's own swatch
  colour for the value where the merchant has set one, otherwise the value's
  name read as a CSS colour, since black, white, navy, grey and the rest are
  colour keywords already. A name that is neither keeps the neutral chip the
  stylesheet paints underneath, so a swatch is never invisible.

  @param value - the product option value

  Usage: {% render 'option-swatch', value: value %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign swatch_color = value.swatch.color
  if swatch_color == blank
    assign swatch_color = value | append: '' | downcase | strip | replace: ' ', ''
  endif
-%}
<span class="option-pill__swatch" aria-hidden="true" style="background-color: {{ swatch_color | escape }};"></span>
